{"id":"p17-l01","minutes":30,"summary":"To a computer an image is a grid of numbers, usually three bytes per pixel. You learn how images are stored as arrays of rows, columns and channels, convert colour to grey and to HSV by hand, see how 8-bit arithmetic silently wraps round, and test your NumPy conversions against OpenCV’s.","html":"<h2 id=\"rows-columns-channels\">Rows, columns, channels</h2>\n<p>A colour image of height <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span> and width <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span></span></span></span> is an array of shape <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>: row first, then column, then channel. Pixel <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is <code>img[r, c]</code>, three numbers from 0 to 255 in an 8-bit (<code>uint8</code>) image. The row index grows <strong>downwards</strong>, so image coordinates have <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span> pointing down. A 640 × 480 colour image is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">640</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">480</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">921</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">600</span></span></span></span> bytes.</p>\n<p>Channel order is a convention. Most libraries use RGB; OpenCV’s image loading returns <strong>BGR</strong>, a historical choice that causes many swapped-colour bugs. Slicing an array (a crop, a flip, one channel) gives a <strong>view</strong> that shares memory with the original rather than a copy.</p>\n<h2 id=\"grey-and-colour-spaces\">Grey and colour spaces</h2>\n<p>A grey (luma) image weights the channels by how bright they look. OpenCV uses the ITU-R BT.601 weights:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.299</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.587</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.114</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p><strong>HSV</strong> separates colour from brightness: value <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">max</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, saturation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">min</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span>, and hue <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span> is an angle around the colour wheel (red 0°, green 120°, blue 240°). Thresholding on hue finds “the red ball” far more reliably under changing light than thresholding RGB. In 8-bit OpenCV images, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span> is stored as degrees divided by 2 so it fits in 0 to 179.</p>\n<h2 id=\"8-bit-arithmetic\">8-bit arithmetic</h2>\n<p><code>uint8</code> arithmetic in NumPy is modulo 256: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">200</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">44</span></span></span></span>. Image libraries <strong>saturate</strong> instead, clipping at 255. Convert to a wider type (<code>int</code> or <code>float</code>) before arithmetic, then clip and convert back.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"pixelinspect\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>An illustrative synthetic image. Move the inspector to read any pixel’s RGB, grey and HSV values, and switch the view between the colour image, its grey version and its separate channels.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>An illustrative 160 × 120 synthetic image: a fading blue sky, a red disc and a green square.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Shape <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">120</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">160</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, <code>uint8</code>, 57 600 bytes.</li>\n<li>The disc pixel at row 60, column 50 is RGB <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">220</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">40</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">30</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. Its grey value is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.299</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">220</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.587</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">40</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.114</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">30</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">92.6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">93</span></span></span></span>. Its HSV is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">220</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">220</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>: hue 4°, a slightly orange red.</li>\n<li>The green square has hue <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">64</span></span></span></span>, i.e. 128°.</li>\n<li>200 + 100 in <code>uint8</code>: NumPy gives 44, saturating arithmetic and <code>cv2.add</code> give 255.</li>\n<li>Against OpenCV: grey and HSV differ by at most 1 level (OpenCV rounds in fixed point), and the nearest-neighbour resize is identical to <code>cv2.INTER_NEAREST_EXACT</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">images.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">try</span>:\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> cv2                                                <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># only used to check our results</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">except</span> ImportError:\n    cv2 = <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">make_image</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">h=<span class=\"hljs-number\">120</span>, w=<span class=\"hljs-number\">160</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;an illustrative synthetic RGB image (uint8, rows x columns x channels): a gradient sky, a red disc, a green square&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    y, x = np.mgrid[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>:h, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>:w]\n    img = np.zeros((h, w, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>), np.uint8)\n    img[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] = (<span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span> * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - y / (h - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>))).astype(np.uint8)          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># blue fades down the image</span>\n    img[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] = (<span class=\"hljs-number\">120</span> * x / (w - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)).astype(np.uint8)\n    disc = (x - <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>)**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> + (y - <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>)**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">25</span>**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    img[disc] = [<span class=\"hljs-number\">220</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>]\n    img[<span class=\"hljs-number\">70</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">105</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">140</span>] = [<span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> img\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">to_gray</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">rgb</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;ITU-R BT.601 luma, the weights OpenCV uses: Y = 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B, rounded&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    r, g, b = [rgb[..., k].astype(np.float64) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.clip(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.299</span> * r + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.587</span> * g + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.114</span> * b), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>).astype(np.uint8)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">to_hsv</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">rgb</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;HSV with OpenCV&#x27;s 8-bit conventions: H in 0..179 (degrees / 2), S and V in 0..255&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    c = rgb.astype(np.float64) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>; r, g, b = c[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], c[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], c[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]\n    v = c.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>); mn = c.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>); d = v - mn\n    s = np.where(v &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, d / np.where(v &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, v, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)\n    dd = np.where(d &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, d, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n    h = np.select([d == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, v == r, v == g], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> * (g - b) / dd, <span class=\"hljs-number\">120</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> * (b - r) / dd], <span class=\"hljs-number\">240</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> * (r - g) / dd)\n    h = np.where(h &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, h + <span class=\"hljs-number\">360</span>, h)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.stack([np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(h / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>) % <span class=\"hljs-number\">180</span>, np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(s * <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>), np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(v * <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>)], -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>).astype(np.uint8)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">resize_nearest</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">img, h, w</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;nearest-neighbour resize: each output pixel copies the source pixel its centre falls in (OpenCV: INTER_NEAREST_EXACT)&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    rows = np.floor((np.arange(h) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>) * img.shape[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] / h).astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>)\n    cols = np.floor((np.arange(w) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>) * img.shape[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] / w).astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> img[rows][:, cols]\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_indexing</span>():\n    img = make_image()\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;shape <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{img.shape}</span> (rows, columns, channels), dtype <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{img.dtype}</span>, <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{img.nbytes}</span> bytes&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;pixel at row 60, column 50 (the disc): RGB <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{img[<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>].tolist()}</span>; at row 0, column 0: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{img[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>].tolist()}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> img[<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>].tolist() == [<span class=\"hljs-number\">220</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> img.shape == (<span class=\"hljs-number\">120</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">160</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)\n    crop = img[<span class=\"hljs-number\">70</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">105</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">140</span>]; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> (crop == [<span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>]).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">all</span>()          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># slicing is a view: no copy</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.shares_memory(crop, img) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> np.array_equal(img[:, ::-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>][:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], img[:, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>])   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># a mirror is just negative strides</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_arithmetic_overflow</span>():\n    a = np.full((<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>, np.uint8); b = np.full((<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>, np.uint8)         <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># two tiny images</span>\n    wrap = (a + b)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]; sat = np.clip(a.astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>) + b, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>).astype(np.uint8)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;uint8 200 + 100: NumPy wraps to <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{wrap}</span>, saturating arithmetic gives <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{sat}</span>&quot;</span> + (<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;, cv2.add gives <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{cv2.add(a, b)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]}</span>&quot;</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> cv2 <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;</span>))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> wrap == <span class=\"hljs-number\">44</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> sat == <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> cv2: <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> cv2.add(a, b)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">255</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_matches_opencv</span>():\n    img = make_image(); g = to_gray(img); hsv = to_hsv(img); small = resize_nearest(img, <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">80</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;gray at the disc <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{g[<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>]}</span>, HSV at the disc <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{hsv[<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>].tolist()}</span>, at the square <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{hsv[<span class=\"hljs-number\">80</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">120</span>].tolist()}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> g[<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.299</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">220</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.587</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">40</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.114</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> cv2 <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">is</span> <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>:\n        <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;OpenCV not installed: skipping the comparison&quot;</span>); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span>\n    dg = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(g.astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>) - cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2GRAY)).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()\n    ref = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2HSV).astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>); dh = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(hsv.astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>) - ref)\n    dh[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] = np.minimum(dh[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">180</span> - dh[..., <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>])                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># hue wraps round</span>\n    dr = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(small.astype(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>) - cv2.resize(img, (<span class=\"hljs-number\">80</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST_EXACT)).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;largest difference from OpenCV: gray <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{dg}</span>, HSV <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{dh.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()}</span> (levels), nearest resize <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{dr}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> dg &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> dh.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> dr == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>\n\ntest_indexing()\ntest_arithmetic_overflow()\ntest_matches_opencv()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does OpenCV’s plain <code>INTER_NEAREST</code> differ from the code’s nearest-neighbour resize when halving an image?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The code samples the source pixel under each output pixel’s <strong>centre</strong>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">⌊(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">⌋</span></span></span></span>, which for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span> is pixel <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7429em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>. Plain <code>INTER_NEAREST</code> uses <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">⌊</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">⌋</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6595em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span></span></span></span>, shifting the image by half an output pixel. <code>INTER_NEAREST_EXACT</code> uses the centre convention.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A red ball under a lamp has RGB <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">200</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">60</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>; in shadow <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">30</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">25</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. Compare their hue and value.</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Both have hue <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">60</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">60</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">200</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4°</span></span></span></span> (and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4°</span></span></span></span> for the shadow) and saturation 0.75. Only the value changes, 200 against 100. A hue threshold catches both; an RGB threshold on red would miss the shadow.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p17-l01\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"rows-columns-channels","title":"Rows, columns, channels"},{"id":"grey-and-colour-spaces","title":"Grey and colour spaces"},{"id":"8-bit-arithmetic","title":"8-bit arithmetic"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p17-l01-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Bytes in a 640 × 480 RGB image at 8 bits per channel?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Width × height × channels.</p>\n","answer":921600,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p17-l01-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Grey value of RGB (100, 200, 50) with the BT.601 weights?</p>\n","explain":"<p>29.9 + 117.4 + 5.7.</p>\n","answer":153,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p17-l01-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>uint8 result of 250 + 10 in NumPy?</p>\n","explain":"<p>It wraps modulo 256.</p>\n","answer":4,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p17-l01-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>OpenCV 8-bit hue value of pure green (120°)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Degrees divided by 2.</p>\n","answer":60,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p17-l01-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>img[10, 20] in a NumPy image is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Rows come first, and rows grow downwards.</p>\n","options":["column 10, row 20","row 10, column 20","x = 10, y = 20","channel 10 of pixel 20"],"answer":1},{"id":"p17-l01-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why threshold on hue rather than on RGB to find a coloured object?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Shadows change V, not H.</p>\n","options":["hue barely changes with brightness","hue is faster to compute","RGB has no red channel in OpenCV","hue has more levels"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"images.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\ntry:\n    import cv2                                                # only used to check our results\nexcept ImportError:\n    cv2 = None\n\ndef make_image(h=120, w=160):\n    \"\"\"an illustrative synthetic RGB image (uint8, rows x columns x channels): a gradient sky, a red disc, a green square\"\"\"\n    y, x = np.mgrid[0:h, 0:w]\n    img = np.zeros((h, w, 3), np.uint8)\n    img[..., 2] = (255 * (1 - y / (h - 1))).astype(np.uint8)          # blue fades down the image\n    img[..., 1] = (120 * x / (w - 1)).astype(np.uint8)\n    disc = (x - 50)**2 + (y - 60)**2 < 25**2\n    img[disc] = [220, 40, 30]\n    img[70:105, 100:140] = [40, 200, 60]\n    return img\n\ndef to_gray(rgb):\n    \"\"\"ITU-R BT.601 luma, the weights OpenCV uses: Y = 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B, rounded\"\"\"\n    r, g, b = [rgb[..., k].astype(np.float64) for k in range(3)]\n    return np.clip(np.round(0.299 * r + 0.587 * g + 0.114 * b), 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n\ndef to_hsv(rgb):\n    \"\"\"HSV with OpenCV's 8-bit conventions: H in 0..179 (degrees / 2), S and V in 0..255\"\"\"\n    c = rgb.astype(np.float64) / 255; r, g, b = c[..., 0], c[..., 1], c[..., 2]\n    v = c.max(-1); mn = c.min(-1); d = v - mn\n    s = np.where(v > 0, d / np.where(v > 0, v, 1), 0)\n    dd = np.where(d > 0, d, 1)\n    h = np.select([d == 0, v == r, v == g], [0, 60 * (g - b) / dd, 120 + 60 * (b - r) / dd], 240 + 60 * (r - g) / dd)\n    h = np.where(h < 0, h + 360, h)\n    return np.stack([np.round(h / 2) % 180, np.round(s * 255), np.round(v * 255)], -1).astype(np.uint8)\n\ndef resize_nearest(img, h, w):\n    \"\"\"nearest-neighbour resize: each output pixel copies the source pixel its centre falls in (OpenCV: INTER_NEAREST_EXACT)\"\"\"\n    rows = np.floor((np.arange(h) + 0.5) * img.shape[0] / h).astype(int)\n    cols = np.floor((np.arange(w) + 0.5) * img.shape[1] / w).astype(int)\n    return img[rows][:, cols]\n\ndef test_indexing():\n    img = make_image()\n    print(f\"shape {img.shape} (rows, columns, channels), dtype {img.dtype}, {img.nbytes} bytes\")\n    print(f\"pixel at row 60, column 50 (the disc): RGB {img[60, 50].tolist()}; at row 0, column 0: {img[0, 0].tolist()}\")\n    assert img[60, 50].tolist() == [220, 40, 30] and img.shape == (120, 160, 3)\n    crop = img[70:105, 100:140]; assert (crop == [40, 200, 60]).all()          # slicing is a view: no copy\n    assert np.shares_memory(crop, img) and np.array_equal(img[:, ::-1][:, 0], img[:, -1])   # a mirror is just negative strides\n\ndef test_arithmetic_overflow():\n    a = np.full((2, 2), 200, np.uint8); b = np.full((2, 2), 100, np.uint8)         # two tiny images\n    wrap = (a + b)[0, 0]; sat = np.clip(a.astype(int) + b, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)[0, 0]\n    print(f\"uint8 200 + 100: NumPy wraps to {wrap}, saturating arithmetic gives {sat}\" + (f\", cv2.add gives {cv2.add(a, b)[0, 0]}\" if cv2 else \"\"))\n    assert wrap == 44 and sat == 255\n    if cv2: assert cv2.add(a, b)[0, 0] == 255\n\ndef test_matches_opencv():\n    img = make_image(); g = to_gray(img); hsv = to_hsv(img); small = resize_nearest(img, 60, 80)\n    print(f\"gray at the disc {g[60, 50]}, HSV at the disc {hsv[60, 50].tolist()}, at the square {hsv[80, 120].tolist()}\")\n    assert g[60, 50] == round(0.299 * 220 + 0.587 * 40 + 0.114 * 30)\n    if cv2 is None:\n        print(\"OpenCV not installed: skipping the comparison\"); return\n    dg = np.abs(g.astype(int) - cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2GRAY)).max()\n    ref = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2HSV).astype(int); dh = np.abs(hsv.astype(int) - ref)\n    dh[..., 0] = np.minimum(dh[..., 0], 180 - dh[..., 0])                    # hue wraps round\n    dr = np.abs(small.astype(int) - cv2.resize(img, (80, 60), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST_EXACT)).max()\n    print(f\"largest difference from OpenCV: gray {dg}, HSV {dh.max()} (levels), nearest resize {dr}\")\n    assert dg <= 1 and dh.max() <= 1 and dr == 0\n\ntest_indexing()\ntest_arithmetic_overflow()\ntest_matches_opencv()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}